 ## 5. Not for now
 
 The voice-tab split is recorded as an open option in [role-process-skill-session.md](/framework/ai/doc/role-process-skill-session.md), no build.
+
+## 6. Built, and what the tab's review of five breakdowns added
+
+- **Built:** the Coverage tab is the chat view (`AISessionCoverage.records_view`): a bubble per prompt with its coverage score, a card per top-level part wearing its module (a per-kind glyph and the module name; the module's own `icon:` is not looked up yet), the outcome tag, the cites (`S4, S7–9`) that show those raw sentences highlighted, and the nested details as a count. Seen headless on four real prompts of session e00f55c9.
+- **Bare follow-ups** ("Make sure that's noted", "Look into it") attach to the part they refer to: a line in `PARTS_BRIEF`. It takes effect after a Servex restart (not yet done at this commit; the landing outcome of the task says when it was), and only for prompts broken down from then on.
+- **Questions, rules and ideas stay "open":** only the `review` process runs the outcomes step. Resolution order: nested parts settle with their parent (computed); run the outcomes step over the ~195 top-level open parts, not the 1,849 (about 90% are nested detail); list what is left per module and settle rules and ideas as notes in that module's doc. Start with session e00f55c9. Not built yet.
+
+- **Review of the branch, answered:** the live `file_cap` is raised from 5 to 15 so a long prompt's asks all become tasks and the tab stays out of it (one writer). The module's own `icon:` is not looked up: no module-name to icon lookup exists, so the card shows the module name with a kind glyph; building the lookup is a follow-up, listed with the chat view. The card is not `InspectCard`, because that draws one object's fields and this card draws a prompt part with cites and a count of its details; both wear an icon and name header, and the Coverage tab stays the one renderer for prompt records (agreed with the deputy: it does not touch `AISessionCoverage.js`). The comparison script keeps the SDK's reported dollars and the map says not to trust the gap; recomputing cost from tokens is queued for the next bulk run. The sample (8 prompts, hand-counted) is stated as small in the map.
